	<Language_en_US>
		<!--===================================================-->
		<!--CONCEPTS-->
		<!--===================================================-->
		<!--Great Relics-->
		<Row Tag="TXT_KEY_JFD_GREAT_RELICS_HEADING1_TITLE">
			<Text>Great Relics</Text>
		</Row>
		<Row Tag="TXT_KEY_JFD_GREAT_RELICS_HEADING1_BODY">
			<Text>[COLOR_POSITIVE_TEXT]Great Relics[ENDCOLOR] are a new type of Great Work that can be acquired by expending a Great Prophet once you have enhanced a Religion. They can only be slotted into the Great Relic Slots provided by the Monastery and Solomon's Temple World Wonder.</Text>
		</Row>
		<!--===================================================-->
		<!--BELIEFS-->
		<!--===================================================-->
		<!--Iconography-->
		<Row Tag="TXT_KEY_BELIEF_JFD_ICONOGRAPHY_SHORT">
			<Text>Iconography</Text>
		</Row>
		<Row Tag="TXT_KEY_BELIEF_JFD_ICONOGRAPHY">
			<Text>+1 [ICON_PEACE] Faith from [ICON_GREAT_WORK] Great Works and [ICON_JFD_RELIC] Relics</Text>
		</Row>
		<!--===================================================-->
		<!--BUILDINGS-->
		<!--===================================================-->
		<!--Monastery-->
		<Row Tag="TXT_KEY_BUILDING_MONASTERY_STRATEGY_JFD_GREAT_RELICS">
			<Text>Monasteries can hold a [ICON_JFD_RELIC] Great Relic, increasing [ICON_CULTURE] Culture and [ICON_TOURISM] Tourism. They also increase a city's [ICON_PEACE] Faith and [ICON_CULTURE] Culture output near to improved Incense and/or Wine resources.</Text>
		</Row>
		<!--===================================================-->
		<!--GREAT PEOPLE-->
		<!--===================================================-->
		<!--Great Prophet-->
		<Row Tag="TXT_KEY_UNIT_HELP_PROPHET_JFD_GREAT_RELICS">
			<Text>The Great Prophet is the only unit who can found, enhance, or reform a religion. He can also construct the special Holy Site improvement which, when worked, produces lots of [ICON_PEACE] Faith. Finally, the Great Prophet can be expended to create a Relic once you have enhanced your Religion. The Great Prophet is expended when used in any of these ways.</Text>
		</Row>
