		</Row>
		<Row Tag="TXT_KEY_WONDER_JFD_SOLOMONS_TEMPLE_HELP">
			<Text>Should this city be captured, the amount of [ICON_GOLD] Gold plundered by the enemy is tripled.</Text>
		</Row>
		<Row Tag="TXT_KEY_WONDER_JFD_SOLOMONS_TEMPLE_QUOTE">
			<Text>[NEWLINE]"All the rivers run into the sea; yet the sea is not full."[NEWLINE] - King Solomon[NEWLINE][TAB]</Text>
		</Row>
		<Row Tag="TXT_KEY_WONDER_JFD_SOLOMONS_TEMPLE_PEDIA">
			<Text>Solomon's Temple, according to the Hebrew Bible, is an ancient, holy temple built by Solomon, King of the Israelites, destroyed by Nebuchadnezzar II of Babylon in his siege of Jersualem in 587 BCE. The Temple was dedicated to the god of Israel, Yahweh, and allegedly housed the legendary Ark of the Covenant. Because of the religious sensivity involved, it is difficult to determine much factual record of the Temple.</Text>
		</Row>
